# Author identity map
#
# Samuel's commits were made under several names across several machines
# (NanoMatch, MelMatch, Sam, match@raman, ...). All of them carry the same
# GitHub no-reply address, so GitHub already links them to one account; this
# file additionally shows a single name in `git shortlog`, `git log` and
# `git blame`.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <email>   (renames every commit with that email)
#
# Anyone committing from a shared machine (the lab PC) must set their own
# identity first — see docs/git_workflow.md. Use your GitHub no-reply address
# (GitHub → Settings → Emails) rather than a personal one: commit emails are
# public, and CI rejects pushes that expose a personal address.
Samuel Brooke <40452389+NanoMatch1@users.noreply.github.com>
